1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:01,640
- Do you want me there with you?

2
00:00:02,440 --> 00:00:03,520
- Come.

3
00:00:04,640 --> 00:00:07,000
- Aren’t you sad at all?

4
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:09,120
- I saw Dad with another woman.

5
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:13,840
- The truth is, our relationship is a lie, too.

6
00:00:14,840 --> 00:00:16,040
- Are you breaking up with me?

7
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:19,680
- Dad taught me love.

8
00:00:20,160 --> 00:00:21,680
- We just have to choose…

9
00:00:21,680 --> 00:00:24,280
- whether to drown in guilt over the past

10
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:27,040
- or find the courage to right our wrongs.

11
00:02:12,280 --> 00:02:13,120
Hold on.

12
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:14,520
What are you doing?

13
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:17,040
Making steak. Why?

14
00:02:18,880 --> 00:02:20,320
You don’t need oil to cook steak.

15
00:02:23,760 --> 00:02:24,600
I know.

16
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:26,000
I don’t need you telling me that.

17
00:02:34,880 --> 00:02:36,600
It’s not cooked yet. Why are you flipping it?

18
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:37,480
Ouch! Shit!

19
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:40,040
Stop talking.
You’re making the oil splatter everywhere.

20
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:41,920
What?

21
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:43,200
Me?

22
00:02:43,440 --> 00:02:44,560
What did I do?

23
00:02:44,920 --> 00:02:47,040
Yes. You’re distracting me.

24
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:49,360
Here, let me do it.

25
00:02:49,480 --> 00:02:50,200
Don’t!

26
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:51,480
If you want to help, do something else.

27
00:02:51,480 --> 00:02:53,120
Get some water or make a salad.
Anything.

28
00:02:53,120 --> 00:02:53,760
No.

29
00:02:53,960 --> 00:02:56,120
I’ll handle the steak,
and you can make the salad.

30
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:07,320
Or we can switch.

31
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:09,200
You make the steak.

32
00:03:09,200 --> 00:03:12,880
And I will… make the salad.

33
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:15,960
That’s more like it.

34
00:03:37,560 --> 00:03:38,360
Nice presentation.

35
00:03:41,079 --> 00:03:42,400
Should we order something in?

36
00:03:42,920 --> 00:03:43,240
Hey.

37
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:45,120
I didn’t say anything.

38
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:46,120
It’s really good.

39
00:03:46,840 --> 00:03:47,680
Can you be a little more honest?

40
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:49,079
How am I not being honest?

41
00:03:50,240 --> 00:03:53,560
Even if you poisoned the food, I’d still eat it.

42
00:03:53,720 --> 00:03:54,120
Yuck!

43
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:55,520
Tone it down a little.

44
00:03:56,280 --> 00:03:57,079
You’re so cheesy.

45
00:03:57,360 --> 00:03:59,640
We’re having steak for lunch.

46
00:03:59,640 --> 00:04:02,240
Japanese food for dinner.

47
00:04:02,760 --> 00:04:04,640
And then late at night…

48
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:08,480
What should we eat?

49
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:14,880
I’m going home.

50
00:04:15,760 --> 00:04:16,200
What?

51
00:04:17,680 --> 00:04:18,680
Why the rush?

52
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:20,399
Stay one more night.

53
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:21,920
One more night?

54
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:24,440
I’ve been staying here since Friday night.

55
00:04:24,760 --> 00:04:25,880
It’s Sunday afternoon already.

56
00:04:27,280 --> 00:04:28,320
Aren’t you gonna let me go home?

57
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:29,920
Isn’t this nice?

58
00:04:30,440 --> 00:04:32,480
You’ll save on water and electricity.

59
00:04:34,200 --> 00:04:35,360
I have work tomorrow morning.

60
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:37,680
Then I’ll just stay at your place instead.

61
00:04:38,720 --> 00:04:39,400
What’s this?

62
00:04:40,040 --> 00:04:41,880
You’re acting like
you don’t have any work to do.

63
00:04:44,320 --> 00:04:45,280
Just stay here.

64
00:04:54,880 --> 00:04:55,600
Eat.

65
00:04:58,760 --> 00:05:00,280
Why don’t you move in with Dean?

66
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:02,080
I don’t know.

67
00:05:03,520 --> 00:05:04,240
Do I have to?

68
00:05:04,600 --> 00:05:06,760
Well, I moved in with Ten.

69
00:05:08,880 --> 00:05:09,960
You and Ten are boyfriends.

70
00:05:13,400 --> 00:05:15,200
Why haven’t you
talked things through with Dean?

71
00:05:17,400 --> 00:05:17,840
I don’t know.

72
00:05:20,640 --> 00:05:21,280
Why not?

73
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:24,280
What’s the problem?

74
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:40,880
He’s calling.

75
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:42,159
Who?

76
00:05:43,080 --> 00:05:43,440
Mes.

77
00:05:52,880 --> 00:05:53,280
What?

78
00:05:53,920 --> 00:05:55,320
You haven’t asked Moth
to be your boyfriend yet?

79
00:05:57,080 --> 00:05:59,200
Moth and I are doing fine.

80
00:05:59,960 --> 00:06:00,840
Why do I have to ask?

81
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:02,440
You need commitment for things like this.

82
00:06:03,160 --> 00:06:04,360
Especially for someone like you.

83
00:06:10,520 --> 00:06:11,000
I think

84
00:06:11,880 --> 00:06:13,640
Moth and I are way past
that boyfriend proposal stage.

85
00:06:16,120 --> 00:06:16,800
It’s not necessary.

86
00:06:18,360 --> 00:06:19,000
Damn you.

87
00:06:19,840 --> 00:06:20,880
You’re always so confident
about the wrong things.

88
00:06:21,320 --> 00:06:23,040
Moth might be waiting for you to ask him.

89
00:06:47,280 --> 00:06:48,880
[WANNA EAT SPICY PORK BONE SOUP.]

90
00:06:53,280 --> 00:06:55,080
[LET’S GO THEN.]

91
00:06:56,920 --> 00:06:59,880
[INCOMING CALL — MES]

92
00:07:08,320 --> 00:07:08,680
Hello.

93
00:07:09,520 --> 00:07:10,920
I thought you wouldn’t pick up.

94
00:07:13,440 --> 00:07:14,600
Is there something you need, Mes?

95
00:07:16,080 --> 00:07:17,400
I’m going back to New York.

96
00:07:18,040 --> 00:07:19,720
(So I wanted to ask you again…)

97
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:22,040
about the artist residency scholarship.

98
00:07:23,400 --> 00:07:23,920
Mes.

99
00:07:24,880 --> 00:07:25,560
About that—

100
00:07:25,560 --> 00:07:26,440
(Hear me out first, Moth.)

101
00:07:27,680 --> 00:07:28,560
Think it over carefully.

102
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:31,040
Don’t turn it down just yet.

103
00:07:35,880 --> 00:07:40,520
If I’ve eve
unintentionally belittled you

104
00:07:41,640 --> 00:07:43,680
or said things that made you doubt

105
00:07:44,280 --> 00:07:46,320
(your comic character illustrations,)

106
00:07:47,440 --> 00:07:48,360
(I’m sorry.)

107
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:51,159
(I really didn’t mean to.

108
00:07:54,880 --> 00:07:56,480
But I want you to ask yourself

109
00:07:57,440 --> 00:07:59,920
(whether you really
want to turn down this opportunity.)

110
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:04,160
(This isn’t about you and me.)

111
00:08:05,200 --> 00:08:07,680
Even if you go and you’re still mad at me,

112
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:10,200
you don’t have to see me at all.

113
00:08:20,560 --> 00:08:21,400
Why don’t you…

114
00:08:24,200 --> 00:08:25,920
talk it over with Dean first

115
00:08:26,320 --> 00:08:27,440
(and give me your answer later?)

116
00:08:29,400 --> 00:08:30,440
What do you mean by that?

117
00:08:31,440 --> 00:08:33,480
(Dean is an important person
in your life, isn’t he?)

118
00:08:34,400 --> 00:08:37,360
(Of course, you should
let him have a say in this.)

119
00:08:42,919 --> 00:08:45,320
Well, yes.

120
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:53,480
I’m glad you’ve found someone
you can trust with your life.

121
00:08:54,680 --> 00:08:59,200
(Honestly, I was really impressed by
what he did at the exhibition that day.)

122
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:01,120
(When he protected you.)

123
00:09:01,840 --> 00:09:02,760
How much is this piece?

124
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:04,200
How much did you sell it for?

125
00:09:04,560 --> 00:09:05,360
I’ll pay double.

126
00:09:05,800 --> 00:09:08,120
This work deserves to be more than just

127
00:09:08,120 --> 00:09:09,760
another meaningless piece
in someone’s collection.

128
00:09:12,480 --> 00:09:14,320
I can’t even imagine myself

129
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:19,200
caring for someone or doing the things
Dean does for you.

130
00:09:22,320 --> 00:09:23,080
(Trust me.)

131
00:09:24,680 --> 00:09:26,480
(Someone as sweet and special as you)

132
00:09:27,560 --> 00:09:33,080
(deserves someone
as loving and caring as him.)

133
00:09:45,440 --> 00:09:46,240
[SPICY PORK BONE SOUP]

134
00:09:46,240 --> 00:09:47,160
This one’s pretty meaty.

135
00:09:47,640 --> 00:09:48,320
Easier to eat.

136
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:51,920
You seem to really like it.

137
00:09:53,400 --> 00:09:54,440
Want me to cook this for you sometime?

138
00:09:55,080 --> 00:09:55,680
Let’s just buy it.

139
00:09:56,320 --> 00:09:57,280
You can’t even cook steak.

140
00:09:59,280 --> 00:10:00,040
Wouldn’t it be nice?

141
00:10:00,560 --> 00:10:01,760
We could spend time cooking together.

142
00:10:04,640 --> 00:10:10,440
Actually, there are other activities
we could do together besides cooking.

143
00:10:11,840 --> 00:10:13,200
those activities…

144
00:10:13,920 --> 00:10:15,080
we can do anytime.

145
00:10:26,880 --> 00:10:27,960
Mes called me today.

146
00:10:29,840 --> 00:10:32,800
He said he’d write me a recommendation
letter for a scholarship in New York.

147
00:10:34,640 --> 00:10:38,200
It’s a program that supports artists
and even provides accommodation.

148
00:10:39,040 --> 00:10:40,320
But I’d have to stay there for a year.

149
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:42,240
Turn him down.

150
00:10:43,120 --> 00:10:45,720
This Mes guy sure is persistent.

151
00:10:55,080 --> 00:10:55,720
Do you want to go?

152
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:03,600
It’s a good opportunity.

153
00:11:05,240 --> 00:11:06,720
I could keep working on
my character illustrations, too.

154
00:11:08,480 --> 00:11:11,040
Can you really do both at the same time?

155
00:11:21,760 --> 00:11:22,480
We can talk about it later.

156
00:11:35,080 --> 00:11:35,920
It’s Friday.

157
00:11:36,800 --> 00:11:38,120
Did someone invite you out partying?

158
00:11:39,920 --> 00:11:40,600
I don’t know.

159
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:43,240
I haven’t gone out with those guys in ages.

160
00:11:44,360 --> 00:11:44,760
Why?

161
00:11:46,520 --> 00:11:47,200
I feel like drinking.

162
00:11:50,640 --> 00:11:51,080
Of course.

163
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:53,040
Let me ask them.

164
00:12:23,840 --> 00:12:26,360
Judging by your face,
you could use a strong drink.

165
00:12:34,680 --> 00:12:35,240
What’s wrong?

166
00:12:36,680 --> 00:12:37,240
Is it about Moth?

167
00:12:37,920 --> 00:12:38,720
Yeah, bro.

168
00:12:40,640 --> 00:12:43,360
Moth’s planning to go abroad.

169
00:12:44,760 --> 00:12:45,720
What should I do?

170
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:51,480
If you don’t want him to go, why not tell him?

171
00:12:53,120 --> 00:12:55,080
It’s his dream. It’s what he wants.

172
00:12:58,840 --> 00:13:00,360
What right do I have to stop him?

173
00:13:02,880 --> 00:13:03,400
Listen, Dean.

174
00:13:04,520 --> 00:13:07,920
Whether you have the right
is for Moth to decide.

175
00:13:08,280 --> 00:13:11,360
You just need to follow your heart.

176
00:13:14,160 --> 00:13:14,840
I’ll be right back.

177
00:13:21,040 --> 00:13:21,840
What are you guys talking about?

178
00:13:23,280 --> 00:13:24,040
Why the long faces?

179
00:13:28,840 --> 00:13:29,320
Nothing.

180
00:13:30,200 --> 00:13:31,320
Let’s head back to our table.

181
00:14:17,480 --> 00:14:19,400
Whoo-hoo!

182
00:14:19,800 --> 00:14:20,720
Careful.

183
00:14:20,880 --> 00:14:21,760
You look hot.

184
00:14:22,440 --> 00:14:23,080
Thanks.

185
00:14:26,920 --> 00:14:29,520
Hey, watch your step.

186
00:14:30,160 --> 00:14:31,000
Look at them.

187
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:34,920
Should we head home now?

188
00:14:35,320 --> 00:14:35,680
Sure.

189
00:14:37,280 --> 00:14:37,880
Let me book a ride.

190
00:14:41,960 --> 00:14:46,080
So, what are you going to do
about Mes’s offer?

191
00:14:50,160 --> 00:14:50,800
I don’t know.

192
00:14:52,520 --> 00:14:54,160
I need to think about it.

193
00:14:57,840 --> 00:14:58,800
Do you want to go?

194
00:15:03,080 --> 00:15:04,160
Be honest with yourself.

195
00:15:06,680 --> 00:15:07,440
Do you want to go?

196
00:15:18,520 --> 00:15:19,960
Honestly…

197
00:15:22,400 --> 00:15:23,280
I do

198
00:15:27,800 --> 00:15:31,680
I’m afraid I’ll regret it
for the rest of my life if I don’t go.

199
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:40,720
What about you?

200
00:15:42,200 --> 00:15:43,080
Do you want me to go?

201
00:15:53,600 --> 00:15:54,280
I think you should.

202
00:15:55,920 --> 00:15:57,000
It’s a great opportunity.

203
00:15:57,520 --> 00:16:00,240
If you decide to go, I wish you all the best.

204
00:16:09,760 --> 00:16:10,560
The ride’s here.

205
00:16:11,720 --> 00:16:12,600
Are you coming home with me tonight?

206
00:16:18,400 --> 00:16:19,120
I’d better not.

207
00:16:19,920 --> 00:16:23,600
I’ve got a headache and feel a little feverish.

208
00:16:24,080 --> 00:16:25,080
I don’t want to give you the flu.

209
00:16:27,520 --> 00:16:28,040
Fine.

210
00:16:29,440 --> 00:16:30,160
I’m heading out, then.

211
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:31,600
I’ll walk you out.

212
00:16:46,040 --> 00:16:46,760
I’m going, then.

213
00:16:47,920 --> 00:16:50,080
Mm. See you.

214
00:16:57,360 --> 00:16:58,520
Get him home safe, sir.

215
00:18:18,760 --> 00:18:19,720
Why are you here?

216
00:18:20,480 --> 00:18:21,160
Can you not go to New York?

217
00:18:27,720 --> 00:18:28,560
What’s with you now?

218
00:18:36,840 --> 00:18:37,640
What the heck are you doing?

219
00:18:39,400 --> 00:18:40,560
Didn’t we already talk about this?

220
00:18:59,440 --> 00:19:00,400
Can you please not go?

221
00:19:22,080 --> 00:19:23,400
Just don’t go.

222
00:19:26,360 --> 00:19:27,120
Please.

223
00:19:34,600 --> 00:19:35,680
Will you stay with me?

224
00:19:50,360 --> 00:19:51,520
You’re not going to leave me, are you?

225
00:20:02,400 --> 00:20:03,240
You won’t, right?

226
00:20:03,720 --> 00:20:04,920
Let’s stay together.

227
00:21:20,440 --> 00:21:24,440
[OUT GETTING MY VISA PHOTOS
AND UNIVERSITY DOCUMENTS.]

228
00:21:24,440 --> 00:21:26,080
[I HAD TO LEAVE EARLY.
DIDN’T WANT TO WAKE YOU.]

229
00:21:26,080 --> 00:21:27,320
[LOCK THE DOOR ON YOUR WAY OUT.]

230
00:21:45,960 --> 00:21:50,760
I’m glad you asked me to stay,

231
00:21:54,720 --> 00:21:57,000
but I think…

232
00:21:59,400 --> 00:22:00,840
I really should go.

233
00:22:19,040 --> 00:22:21,200
I want to be true to my heart,

234
00:22:24,440 --> 00:22:27,760
and it’s telling me.

235
00:22:34,200 --> 00:22:35,920
I shouldn’t let this opportunity pass me by.

236
00:22:52,320 --> 00:22:54,200
Don’t I have a place in your heart at all?

237
00:23:07,120 --> 00:23:08,720
I’ll only be gone for a year.

238
00:23:11,680 --> 00:23:12,840
I’ll be back before you know it.

239
00:23:20,200 --> 00:23:21,400
Are you sure

240
00:23:25,880 --> 00:23:31,160
things will still be the same a year from now?

241
00:23:32,880 --> 00:23:37,160
♪ Maybe I just love you that much ♪

242
00:23:38,880 --> 00:23:43,160
♪ So I get what’s happening to us ♪

243
00:23:43,160 --> 00:23:47,440
♪ Though I want you to stay ♪

244
00:23:48,320 --> 00:23:53,920
♪ Today I have to let you walk away ♪

245
00:23:56,800 --> 00:24:01,480
♪ No matter how much I love you,
It’s pointless ♪

246
00:24:02,400 --> 00:24:06,640
♪ I’ll let reality win,
Though my heart protests ♪

247
00:24:06,640 --> 00:24:11,800
♪ A thousand words of love
Make no difference ♪

248
00:24:11,800 --> 00:24:16,480
♪ This is where it ends ♪

249
00:24:31,680 --> 00:24:32,400
Go.

250
00:24:34,600 --> 00:24:36,200
Honestly, I’m so glad

251
00:24:38,800 --> 00:24:43,360
you’re doing what you love
and following your dreams.

252
00:24:55,040 --> 00:24:56,360
I’ll be waiting for you here.

253
00:24:59,960 --> 00:25:04,560
♪ I want to hug you one more time ♪

254
00:25:04,560 --> 00:25:10,240
♪ To remind me that once upon a time♪

255
00:25:10,240 --> 00:25:12,760
♪ We met and our hearts beat in rhyme ♪

256
00:25:12,760 --> 00:25:16,000
♪ Before you leave my arms tomorrow ♪

257
00:25:16,000 --> 00:25:18,680
♪ Before the word love has nowhere to go ♪

258
00:25:18,680 --> 00:25:22,720
♪ Even if tonight’s the last time ♪

259
00:25:22,720 --> 00:25:27,480
♪ I get to say I love you ♪

260
00:25:41,280 --> 00:25:45,720
♪ Even if tonight’s the last time ♪

261
00:26:08,880 --> 00:26:09,800
[THE DOOR IS LOCKED.]

262
00:26:09,800 --> 00:26:10,800
[MHM.]

263
00:26:10,800 --> 00:26:12,240
[LET ME KNOW WHEN YOU GET HOME.]

264
00:26:26,800 --> 00:26:28,920
Cheers!

265
00:26:30,240 --> 00:26:32,120
The lights are gorgeous tonight.

266
00:26:33,400 --> 00:26:34,560
Good luck, Moth.

267
00:26:35,320 --> 00:26:37,600
If things work out for you there,
just stay there.

268
00:26:37,600 --> 00:26:38,440
Don’t come back.

269
00:26:39,560 --> 00:26:41,040
That doesn’t sound much like a wish.

270
00:26:41,680 --> 00:26:42,520
You’re basically telling me to get lost.

271
00:26:43,720 --> 00:26:46,400
If you can start a new life abroad,
then just stay there.

272
00:26:46,520 --> 00:26:47,600
Come on, bro.

273
00:26:47,720 --> 00:26:49,240
Don’t say that. I feel bad for Dean.

274
00:26:49,320 --> 00:26:50,320
Why would you feel bad for him?

275
00:26:51,040 --> 00:26:52,760
And seriously, what the hell?

276
00:26:52,760 --> 00:26:55,880
We’re throwing Moth a going-away party,
and that jackass doesn’t even show up.

277
00:26:56,480 --> 00:26:58,440
He’s busy with work.

278
00:26:58,840 --> 00:27:00,960
Honestly, I don’t get him these days.

279
00:27:01,280 --> 00:27:02,560
He keeps turning down my invitations.

280
00:27:02,560 --> 00:27:03,520
Gosh, I’m so pissed.

281
00:27:18,280 --> 00:27:23,200
Today, Pun and I threw Moth
a going-away party.

282
00:27:25,360 --> 00:27:27,760
He said he’d go
partying with your friends afterward.

283
00:27:28,400 --> 00:27:33,280
Tomorrow, he’s going to Phuket
to be with his parents

284
00:27:33,720 --> 00:27:35,160
before flying to New York.

285
00:27:40,800 --> 00:27:41,480
Yeah?

286
00:27:43,920 --> 00:27:44,400
Mm.

287
00:27:46,400 --> 00:27:47,440
Moth is leaving.

288
00:27:48,240 --> 00:27:49,480
Aren’t you going to see him?

289
00:27:51,560 --> 00:27:52,560
It’s better if I don’t.

290
00:27:54,120 --> 00:27:58,000
If we’re going our separate ways,
we might as well start now.

291
00:27:59,280 --> 00:27:59,840
It’s for the best.

292
00:28:00,800 --> 00:28:03,800
You say you don’t want to see him,
but you’re on his Instagram all day.

293
00:28:08,840 --> 00:28:12,440
Not to mention
you’ve been tailing Moth all month.

294
00:28:12,800 --> 00:28:15,280
I could be on another planet
and still tell how much you miss him.

295
00:28:15,840 --> 00:28:18,240
Why are you moping around
like some guy in a music video?

296
00:28:18,680 --> 00:28:20,000
Just go see him and get it over with.

297
00:28:21,600 --> 00:28:24,640
I’m not seeing him
because I’m trying to control myself.

298
00:28:26,960 --> 00:28:30,320
Being away from him
is already driving me insane.

299
00:28:33,040 --> 00:28:39,600
What if Moth changes his mind one day
and gets together with someone else?

300
00:28:42,520 --> 00:28:43,760
Don’t you know that I could f*cking die?

301
00:28:44,080 --> 00:28:44,520
Huh?

302
00:28:46,520 --> 00:28:49,320
I’m doing this to protect myself.

303
00:28:50,600 --> 00:28:51,640
To keep myself from losing my mind.

304
00:28:56,400 --> 00:28:57,720
Can you hear yourself?

305
00:28:58,440 --> 00:28:59,600
You realize how much you love Moth?

306
00:28:59,600 --> 00:29:00,120
Yes!

307
00:29:01,840 --> 00:29:04,480
I know. I admit it. I love Moth so much.

308
00:29:05,400 --> 00:29:06,640
I love him so much it’s driving me crazy.

309
00:29:07,240 --> 00:29:09,080
But what can I do, huh?

310
00:29:09,880 --> 00:29:11,000
What the f*ck can I do?

311
00:29:12,400 --> 00:29:14,440
I tried everything to stop him.
Every damn thing.

312
00:29:14,440 --> 00:29:16,280
really tried it all.

313
00:29:19,640 --> 00:29:20,960
There’s nothing else I can do.

314
00:29:22,840 --> 00:29:23,840
Do you understand?

315
00:29:28,160 --> 00:29:31,720
Are you sure you’ve done everything?

316
00:29:33,920 --> 00:29:35,120
You said it yourself.

317
00:29:36,200 --> 00:29:37,520
You love him so much you’re going crazy.

318
00:29:38,360 --> 00:29:39,400
You don’t want to lose him.

319
00:29:40,720 --> 00:29:44,120
So are you sure you’ve done everything?

320
00:29:58,080 --> 00:29:58,600
Hey!

321
00:29:59,080 --> 00:29:59,840
Where are you going?

322
00:30:23,360 --> 00:30:33,280
[MANIAC]

323
00:30:37,320 --> 00:30:38,040
Hello.

324
00:30:38,360 --> 00:30:38,920
Where are you?

325
00:30:38,920 --> 00:30:39,520
(What did you say?)

326
00:30:40,280 --> 00:30:42,080
Where are you?
It’s so loud. I can’t hear you.

327
00:30:42,080 --> 00:30:42,840
(I’m at the club.)

328
00:30:43,440 --> 00:30:44,080
Hello?

329
00:30:44,280 --> 00:30:45,160
I’m at the club.

330
00:30:46,680 --> 00:30:47,440
Are you coming?

331
00:30:47,800 --> 00:30:50,160
Listen. I’m sorry I disappeared.

332
00:30:50,520 --> 00:30:51,440
I can’t hear you.

333
00:30:51,680 --> 00:30:52,320
Hello?

334
00:30:53,960 --> 00:30:54,600
Did you say something?

335
00:30:55,120 --> 00:30:56,520
I was just scared I’d lose my mind.

336
00:30:56,680 --> 00:30:58,320
So I tried to disappear from your life.

337
00:30:59,960 --> 00:31:01,360
I tried, but it really didn’t work.

338
00:31:01,360 --> 00:31:03,400
(I love you so much. I’m sorry.)

339
00:31:05,840 --> 00:31:07,000
What did you just say?

340
00:31:08,400 --> 00:31:11,360
I said I’m sorry I disappeared.

341
00:31:12,600 --> 00:31:16,000
(I tried to disappear from your life,
but it really didn’t work.)

342
00:31:17,160 --> 00:31:17,920
I’m sorry.

343
00:31:19,440 --> 00:31:20,800
It’s because I love you so much.

344
00:31:23,600 --> 00:31:23,920
Moth.

345
00:31:25,680 --> 00:31:26,000
Moth?

346
00:31:26,600 --> 00:31:27,240
Can you hear me?

347
00:31:29,160 --> 00:31:30,160
Damn it!

348
00:31:30,440 --> 00:31:31,840
The light’s green! Why aren’t you going?

349
00:31:34,600 --> 00:31:36,040
Hey! Where’s Moth?

350
00:31:36,040 --> 00:31:37,440
Wow, took you long enough, dude.

351
00:31:37,440 --> 00:31:39,120
Come on. Have a drink with us.

352
00:31:39,120 --> 00:31:39,720
I’m not drinking.

353
00:31:39,720 --> 00:31:40,400
Where’s Moth?

354
00:31:40,400 --> 00:31:41,240
Just have a little.

355
00:31:41,240 --> 00:31:42,160
Let go of me.

356
00:31:42,960 --> 00:31:44,080
Hey, Dean.

357
00:31:44,920 --> 00:31:45,560
Have you seen Moth?

358
00:31:45,760 --> 00:31:46,360
He left.

359
00:31:46,360 --> 00:31:48,240
He said he had to leave town tomorrow.

360
00:31:49,840 --> 00:31:50,560
Shit.

361
00:31:52,840 --> 00:31:54,280
- Ohm.
- Hm?

362
00:31:54,520 --> 00:31:55,480
Scan your face.

363
00:31:55,880 --> 00:31:57,160
Face scan complete!

364
00:31:57,880 --> 00:31:59,120
What do you need my phone for, anyway?

365
00:31:59,920 --> 00:32:01,560
There’s no way Ohm has Moth’s number.

366
00:32:01,960 --> 00:32:03,160
I remember every single digit.

367
00:32:16,680 --> 00:32:17,320
Hello.

368
00:32:17,560 --> 00:32:18,640
(Hello. Where are you?)

369
00:32:20,600 --> 00:32:21,080
Dean!

370
00:32:22,320 --> 00:32:22,920
Is that you, Dean?

371
00:32:23,280 --> 00:32:24,200
Yeah. Where are you?

372
00:32:24,200 --> 00:32:25,000
(I can’t hear you.)

373
00:32:26,080 --> 00:32:26,960
(Are you at the club?)

374
00:32:27,160 --> 00:32:29,440
Yes. I thought you were here, so I came.

375
00:32:31,800 --> 00:32:33,240
I’ll tell the driver to turn around.

376
00:32:33,360 --> 00:32:33,680
No need.

377
00:32:33,680 --> 00:32:35,440
It’s too crowded here.

378
00:32:35,440 --> 00:32:36,240
Let’s talk somewhere else.

379
00:32:36,960 --> 00:32:38,000
How about my place?

380
00:32:38,000 --> 00:32:38,960
How long until you get home?

381
00:32:39,680 --> 00:32:40,840
(About an hour.)

382
00:32:41,080 --> 00:32:42,280
Then get out now.

383
00:32:42,280 --> 00:32:43,560
Send me your location. I’ll come to you.

384
00:32:43,560 --> 00:32:44,240
Now.

385
00:32:44,960 --> 00:32:46,120
Shouldn’t we just meet at home?

386
00:32:46,120 --> 00:32:46,520
No!

387
00:32:47,440 --> 00:32:48,960
I want to see you as soon as possible.

388
00:32:49,240 --> 00:32:52,480
I don’t want to waste any more time.
Not even for another second.

389
00:33:12,280 --> 00:33:12,720
Hey!

390
00:33:13,240 --> 00:33:14,280
My phone

391
00:33:51,760 --> 00:33:52,920
What the hell was I thinking?

392
00:33:54,120 --> 00:33:55,160
Who would wait for me?

393
00:34:41,239 --> 00:34:42,239
Are you crazy?

394
00:34:43,400 --> 00:34:44,719
You suddenly told me to get out of the car.

395
00:34:45,520 --> 00:34:46,560
Yeah, I’m crazy because of you.

396
00:34:47,000 --> 00:34:47,840
I missed you like crazy.

397
00:34:48,120 --> 00:34:48,880
I’m crazy in love with you.

398
00:34:48,880 --> 00:34:49,600
I was going crazy wanting to see you.

399
00:34:49,880 --> 00:34:50,800
I’m crazy about everything.

400
00:35:03,280 --> 00:35:06,880
I couldn’t stand the idea of
being apart from you.

401
00:35:08,520 --> 00:35:09,840
So I tried to disappear from your life.

402
00:35:12,480 --> 00:35:14,280
But I never expected it to hurt this much.

403
00:35:18,520 --> 00:35:19,400
I’m sorry.

404
00:35:24,720 --> 00:35:29,640
I’m sorry I can’t give you
what you asked for,

405
00:35:34,960 --> 00:35:35,360
but…

406
00:35:39,000 --> 00:35:40,640
Can I give you my promise instead?

407
00:35:45,960 --> 00:35:54,520
I understand if you don’t want to hear it
or believe my promises.

408
00:35:59,880 --> 00:36:04,360
But even if we’re apart,
I’ll miss you every day,

409
00:36:05,160 --> 00:36:05,960
very hour,

410
00:36:08,400 --> 00:36:09,520
and every minute.

411
00:36:11,800 --> 00:36:13,920
I’ll miss you to my very bones until I go crazy.

412
00:36:17,040 --> 00:36:23,800
So, will you wait for me?

413
00:36:32,240 --> 00:36:36,280
All this time, I thought…

414
00:36:40,120 --> 00:36:41,600
I’d done everything I could
to keep you from leaving.

415
00:36:48,440 --> 00:36:49,200
But I…

416
00:36:53,840 --> 00:36:57,560
I haven’t really tried everything.

417
00:37:12,920 --> 00:37:13,560
What are you doing?

418
00:37:16,240 --> 00:37:17,440
Asking you to be my boyfriend.

419
00:37:22,840 --> 00:37:23,280
Moth.

420
00:37:27,760 --> 00:37:28,720
Will you be my boyfriend?

421
00:37:32,320 --> 00:37:36,000
You can study wherever you want,

422
00:37:37,400 --> 00:37:40,680
but if you agree to be my boyfriend today,

423
00:37:43,640 --> 00:37:48,120
I’ll wait for you, no matter how long it takes.

424
00:37:51,720 --> 00:37:52,760
I know

425
00:37:54,520 --> 00:38:01,160
distance and time won’t change how I feel.

426
00:38:06,080 --> 00:38:06,920
So

427
00:38:09,640 --> 00:38:10,760
If we’re on the same page,

428
00:38:15,880 --> 00:38:16,920
please be my boyfriend.

429
00:38:20,000 --> 00:38:21,600
You’re already kneeling
to ask me to be your boyfriend.

430
00:38:22,800 --> 00:38:24,120
What are you gonna do
when it’s time to propose marriage?

431
00:38:24,120 --> 00:38:24,880
I have no idea.

432
00:38:25,800 --> 00:38:27,000
I’ll figure that out when the time comes.

433
00:38:27,440 --> 00:38:28,640
So, what’s your answer?

434
00:38:32,280 --> 00:38:35,360
After everything I just said,
isn’t my answer obvious?

435
00:38:39,480 --> 00:38:40,080
Yes.

436
00:39:13,200 --> 00:39:13,600
Wait.

437
00:39:14,760 --> 00:39:15,320
But…

438
00:39:16,320 --> 00:39:17,880
I haven’t thought
that far ahead to marriage yet.

439
00:39:19,680 --> 00:39:20,480
Can we…

440
00:39:24,400 --> 00:39:25,800
take it one step at a time?

441
00:39:28,120 --> 00:39:29,080
Don’t rush it.

442
00:39:30,640 --> 00:39:31,800
Who said anything about marriage?

443
00:39:32,840 --> 00:39:34,600
- You’re nuts.
- What? You just did!

444
00:39:35,760 --> 00:39:36,400
No, I didn’t.

445
00:39:37,160 --> 00:39:37,640
Then who did?

446
00:39:38,680 --> 00:39:40,400
The boat? The water?

447
00:39:40,680 --> 00:39:41,200
Who?

448
00:39:43,360 --> 00:39:44,360
You maniac.

449
00:39:45,040 --> 00:39:45,720
That’s cute.

450
00:39:47,200 --> 00:39:48,440
Can you say that again?

451
00:39:49,240 --> 00:39:49,800
Maniac.

452
00:39:50,360 --> 00:39:51,360
I didn’t catch that.

453
00:39:51,680 --> 00:39:52,640
Can you say it again?

454
00:39:52,800 --> 00:39:53,480
You maniac!

455
00:39:53,640 --> 00:39:54,280
I love it when you yell at me.

456
00:39:54,280 --> 00:39:55,440
Can you say it loud and clear?

457
00:39:55,440 --> 00:39:56,160
Dean, you maniac!

458
00:39:56,240 --> 00:39:56,720
What?

459
00:39:56,720 --> 00:39:58,200
Stop being so crazy, you crazy—

460
00:40:09,360 --> 00:40:10,280
Maniac.

461
00:40:11,160 --> 00:40:11,720
I know.

462
00:40:12,840 --> 00:40:14,360
I know you love a maniac like me.

463
00:40:42,440 --> 00:40:45,760
THREE YEARS LATER

464
00:41:30,760 --> 00:41:31,720
Wow.

465
00:41:32,680 --> 00:41:34,000
You don’t burn eggs anymore.

466
00:41:36,320 --> 00:41:38,360
Well, humans are built to evolve.

467
00:41:42,800 --> 00:41:43,680
Are you making fried rice?

468
00:41:44,360 --> 00:41:44,840
Let me do it.

469
00:41:45,160 --> 00:41:47,160
It’s fine. I’ve got this.

470
00:41:48,440 --> 00:41:48,760
What?

471
00:41:49,760 --> 00:41:50,720
Are you worried it won’t taste good?

472
00:41:51,120 --> 00:41:53,640
Of course it’ll taste good. I didn’t say that.

473
00:41:56,720 --> 00:41:58,920
My boyfriend’s cooking is always delicious.

474
00:41:59,560 --> 00:41:59,880
That’s right.

475
00:42:01,400 --> 00:42:03,000
Even if it doesn’t taste good,
you still have to eat it.

476
00:42:04,280 --> 00:42:05,280
Because I’m doing my best.

477
00:42:18,920 --> 00:42:23,280
How many times have I told you
to wear an apron whenever you cook?

478
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:31,240
What if you get your T-shirt dirty?

479
00:42:32,480 --> 00:42:33,640
It’s limited edition.

480
00:42:33,800 --> 00:42:35,080
It’s not easy to get.

481
00:42:35,760 --> 00:42:37,000
You can’t buy it anywhere.

482
00:42:37,120 --> 00:42:41,360
Limited edition
because nobody pre-ordered it, right?

483
00:42:42,800 --> 00:42:43,480
I’m kidding.

484
00:42:53,600 --> 00:42:55,040
Hey, I’m cooking here.

485
00:42:56,640 --> 00:42:58,280
Then keep cooking.

486
00:43:00,040 --> 00:43:03,080
I’ll just use my boyfriend
to recharge my energy.

487
00:43:04,400 --> 00:43:05,200
Dean!

488
00:43:08,000 --> 00:43:09,080
Go sit down and wait.

489
00:43:11,840 --> 00:43:12,720
You’re so mean.

490
00:43:13,560 --> 00:43:14,560
It’s not like I’m asking for much.

491
00:43:30,920 --> 00:43:32,240
Let’s see, Chef.

492
00:43:32,240 --> 00:43:33,240
What are you making?

493
00:43:33,320 --> 00:43:34,600
Does that look like spaghetti to you?

494
00:43:49,840 --> 00:43:51,960
Dr. Pun is opening a new branch next week.

495
00:43:52,120 --> 00:43:54,800
You promised you’d do a review.

496
00:43:55,120 --> 00:43:56,400
I’ve already scheduled the date and time.

497
00:43:57,920 --> 00:44:00,360
Sorry to trouble you, Mr. 10M Reviewer.

498
00:44:02,480 --> 00:44:03,760
It’s no trouble at all.

499
00:44:03,960 --> 00:44:05,080
Just think of him as your friend’s boyfriend.

500
00:44:06,080 --> 00:44:08,840
Don’t feel bad. He’s gotta do it for you.

501
00:44:09,720 --> 00:44:10,160
Wow.

502
00:44:11,120 --> 00:44:14,560
You’ve really leveled up
since you got together with Dr. Pun.

503
00:44:17,280 --> 00:44:20,960
So this is what it feels like
to see a friend start a family.

504
00:44:22,160 --> 00:44:27,200
It’s just that your kid has four legs
and likes sticking her tongue out.

505
00:44:27,480 --> 00:44:28,920
- Don’t disrespect my child!
- Don’t disrespect my child!

506
00:44:29,120 --> 00:44:30,240
Aw. Your child?

507
00:44:31,640 --> 00:44:33,040
Go over there.

508
00:44:33,040 --> 00:44:34,360
Bite him!

509
00:44:34,360 --> 00:44:35,040
Finish him off!

510
00:44:35,040 --> 00:44:37,080
- Get him, girl.
- Take him.

511
00:44:37,280 --> 00:44:38,280
Keep your boyfriend in check.

512
00:44:38,760 --> 00:44:39,520
I will.

513
00:44:39,920 --> 00:44:41,200
Your kid keeps messing with me.

514
00:44:43,440 --> 00:44:44,400
It’s not just Dean.

515
00:44:45,800 --> 00:44:47,400
I feel that way, too.

516
00:44:49,040 --> 00:44:49,400
What?

517
00:44:50,320 --> 00:44:51,920
Seeing a friend start a family.

518
00:44:53,400 --> 00:44:54,760
There’s a couple right in front of me.

519
00:44:55,280 --> 00:44:56,760
Nope. You’re wrong.

520
00:45:01,440 --> 00:45:02,960
Fine, you’re right.

521
00:45:04,720 --> 00:45:05,720
Try to get used to it.

522
00:45:06,560 --> 00:45:10,320
I’m happy you two finally got together.

523
00:45:11,800 --> 00:45:13,080
I thought it’d happen after I died.

524
00:45:15,160 --> 00:45:17,560
Honestly, I never thought
we’d get to this day.

525
00:45:18,560 --> 00:45:21,200
But what could I do? I couldn’t resist him.

526
00:45:22,320 --> 00:45:23,400
I really love him.

527
00:45:26,480 --> 00:45:27,800
Stop indulging your friend.

528
00:45:30,120 --> 00:45:30,640
Moth.

529
00:45:32,400 --> 00:45:34,240
Are you back for good this time?

530
00:45:35,920 --> 00:45:36,920
Um...

531
00:45:38,760 --> 00:45:42,040
Actually, a lot of companies
have offered me jobs,

532
00:45:42,840 --> 00:45:46,000
and there are many galleries
where I want to exhibit my work.

533
00:45:46,640 --> 00:45:47,400
But I’ve talked to them,

534
00:45:47,400 --> 00:45:51,480
and they said I could stay in Thailand
and send them my work.

535
00:45:51,480 --> 00:45:53,720
Kind of like a hybrid arrangement.

536
00:45:53,960 --> 00:45:54,560
Yes!

537
00:45:55,240 --> 00:45:56,120
That’s perfect.

538
00:46:03,560 --> 00:46:03,920
What?

539
00:46:05,480 --> 00:46:06,400
Why are you all looking at me?

540
00:46:07,320 --> 00:46:08,400
Have you never seen
a happy person before?

541
00:46:11,960 --> 00:46:13,920
Thank you for choosing me.

542
00:46:19,560 --> 00:46:20,600
I didn’t choose you.

543
00:46:22,520 --> 00:46:24,520
I just chose what’s best for me.

544
00:46:27,760 --> 00:46:31,720
We’re together, after all.
I don’t want us to be apart forever.

545
00:46:33,880 --> 00:46:35,200
When I miss you,

546
00:46:35,920 --> 00:46:37,720
I want to share those little moments
that other couples get to have.

547
00:46:38,280 --> 00:46:39,520
Oh, wow!

548
00:46:40,560 --> 00:46:44,120
You finally said something sweet for once.

549
00:46:45,600 --> 00:46:48,320
As if you’ve never had your own dark phase,

550
00:46:48,760 --> 00:46:49,440
Mr…

551
00:46:53,160 --> 00:46:54,400
Monsieur?

552
00:46:54,880 --> 00:46:56,120
Monsieur. Monsieur.

553
00:46:56,120 --> 00:46:57,600
Yes, Mr. Monsieur.

554
00:46:57,960 --> 00:46:58,720
Monsieur.

555
00:46:58,880 --> 00:47:00,160
Damn you!

556
00:47:59,840 --> 00:48:02,160
Thanks for coming with me to visit my mom.

557
00:48:03,680 --> 00:48:04,520
Why are you thanking me?

558
00:48:05,680 --> 00:48:06,960
I really like your mom.

559
00:48:08,560 --> 00:48:11,560
She’s sweet and a great cook.

560
00:48:13,520 --> 00:48:15,760
If you like her so much,
why don’t you move here?

561
00:48:27,880 --> 00:48:30,160
Are you serious?

562
00:48:31,320 --> 00:48:31,880
I’m kidding.

563
00:48:33,880 --> 00:48:35,600
A city boy like you
could never live in the countryside.

564
00:48:36,160 --> 00:48:36,760
You couldn’t.

565
00:48:38,280 --> 00:48:39,120
Think about it.

566
00:48:39,920 --> 00:48:41,280
Who exactly couldn’t live here?

567
00:48:42,640 --> 00:48:44,720
You’re more attached to city life than I am.

568
00:48:45,640 --> 00:48:49,480
Actually, I could bring my work here
and stay at your mom’s house for a month.

569
00:48:53,600 --> 00:48:57,760
Well, I used to be captivated by city life,

570
00:49:00,360 --> 00:49:03,280
but now I think
I’m captivated by something else.

571
00:49:04,240 --> 00:49:06,360
Please don’t finish that sentence.

572
00:49:06,360 --> 00:49:07,960
I’m completely captivated by my boyfriend.

573
00:49:09,360 --> 00:49:12,320
If my boyfriend doesn’t live here,
then neither do I.

574
00:49:21,840 --> 00:49:26,440
Back then, I couldn’t even imagine myself
being in a relationship.

575
00:49:34,520 --> 00:49:38,560
Thank you for coming into my life.

576
00:49:52,880 --> 00:49:54,840
I never came into your life.

577
00:49:56,520 --> 00:49:59,280
You’re the one who came into mine first.

578
00:50:01,520 --> 00:50:02,760
I’m grateful to you anyway

579
00:50:04,360 --> 00:50:07,840
for choosing to stay in my life

580
00:50:08,840 --> 00:50:15,080
when a coward like me
didn’t even dare to think about love.

581
00:50:21,160 --> 00:50:21,680
Mm.

582
00:50:24,040 --> 00:50:25,600
I’m grateful to you, too,

583
00:50:27,040 --> 00:50:29,400
for making me realize that

584
00:50:31,240 --> 00:50:34,160
I deserve love, too,

585
00:50:36,040 --> 00:50:44,040
and for making me feel like
someone sees my worth.

586
00:50:51,760 --> 00:50:55,600
Even though you’re not
what I imagined my partner would be like.

587
00:50:56,040 --> 00:50:58,760
Wait. What?

588
00:50:59,280 --> 00:50:59,920
What’s wrong with me?

589
00:51:00,400 --> 00:51:02,280
I’m nothing like the partner
you imagined at all?

590
00:51:02,440 --> 00:51:02,800
Huh?

591
00:51:04,240 --> 00:51:05,680
It’s not like you’re that different.

592
00:51:06,400 --> 00:51:09,640
I just never thought I’d end up with a maniac.

593
00:51:13,920 --> 00:51:19,040
It’s hard to believe
two maniacs like us could fall in love.

594
00:51:20,600 --> 00:51:23,680
Nothing makes more sense than
two maniacs like us falling in love.

595
00:51:24,400 --> 00:51:25,320
There’s no other way.
